-- SEQUENCING TRAP — read before adding a SECOND "real admin_user_id" row
-- anywhere in this file or a future one.
-- ===========================================================================
-- parity.mjs's seedDatabase() (which runs every file in FIXTURE_FILES,
-- INCLUDING THIS ONE) executes strictly BEFORE fireThrowawayProbeRequest()
-- and seedAdminUser() (see parity.mjs's main() — the exact order is
-- composeUp -> waitContainerHealthy(mariadb) -> waitContainerHealthy(redis)
-- -> seedDatabase() -> waitHttpReachable('/') -> fireThrowawayProbeRequest()
-- -> generatePhpBcryptHash() -> seedAdminUser()). `admin_users` does NOT
-- exist in the committed tenant template (deliberately excluded — see
-- infra/e2e/seed/20-admin-user.sql.tmpl's own header comment, and
-- database/migration_2026-05-25_tenant_template.sql's own header note that
-- platform-level tables live in `reya_platform`) and is only auto-created by
-- classes/AdminAuth.php's constructor fallback (ensureTables(), lines
-- 32-72), which only runs the FIRST time includes/auth_check.php
-- instantiates `new AdminAuth($db)` on a real page load — against
-- `Database::getInstance()->getConnection()`, i.e. the CURRENT TENANT DB
-- (bootstrap/resolve_subdomain.php's resolution), the SAME physical database
-- this file's own INSERTs below land in — i.e. NOT yet, at the point THIS
-- file's INSERTs run. Two consequences, both verified by reading
-- classes/AdminAuth.php, includes/auth_check.php,
-- infra/e2e/seed/20-admin-user.sql.tmpl, and parity.mjs's main() in full
-- (not guessed):
--
--   1. This file CANNOT `SELECT id FROM admin_users WHERE username = ...`
--      in a subquery — the table doesn't exist yet at this point in the
--      sequence and such a statement would abort the whole seeding run.
--      `data_access_logs.admin_user_id` has NO foreign-key constraint
--      (plain `int(11) DEFAULT NULL`, confirmed by reading the tenant
--      template's CREATE TABLE) so a literal integer is safe to insert here
--      even though no admin_users row with that id exists YET — the FK-like
--      relationship is only ever read via consent.php's own
--      `LEFT JOIN admin_users au ON dal.admin_user_id = au.id`, which
--      doesn't run until the actual page fetch, long after
--      fireThrowawayProbeRequest()/seedAdminUser() have both completed —
--      by which point `admin_users` genuinely exists IN THIS SAME DB (see
--      point 2's own note on the runtime-auto-create-vs-committed-template
--      distinction — this matters a great deal for how
--      extractSettingsConsentTab() is designed; see that function's own
--      module doc in infra/e2e/lib/extract.mjs and this batch's runbook).
--
--   2. The literal id to use for "the harness's own real admin" is
--      DETERMINISTIC, not guessed: AdminAuth::ensureTables() (lines 34-43)
--      tries `SELECT 1 FROM admin_users LIMIT 1` first; on a fresh DB that
--      throws (table doesn't exist), so the `catch` block (lines 44-71)
--      creates the table AND does exactly ONE
--      `INSERT IGNORE INTO admin_users (username, ...) VALUES ('admin', ...)`
--      (line 65-68) — this is the FIRST ever row, so it gets id=1.
--      `fireThrowawayProbeRequest()` (an unauthenticated GET to
--      /system-status.php) is the FIRST request in the whole harness run
--      that reaches includes/auth_check.php's unconditional
--      `new AdminAuth($db)` (auth_check.php line 17, instantiated BEFORE the
--      `isset($_SESSION['admin_user'])` gate, so it fires even for a
--      logged-out request) — nothing earlier in parity.mjs's sequence hits
--      any auth_check.php-gated PHP page. Immediately after that,
--      seedAdminUser() applies infra/e2e/seed/20-admin-user.sql.tmpl, which
--      does `DELETE FROM admin_users WHERE username = '__ADMIN_USERNAME__'`
--      (a no-op — different username, nothing to delete) then
--      `INSERT INTO admin_users (username, ...) VALUES ('__ADMIN_USERNAME__' /* e2e_parity_admin */, ...)`
--      — the SECOND row ever inserted into a freshly-created table, so it
--      deterministically gets id=2. `docker compose down -v` in
--      parity.mjs's finally block (composeDown()) removes the MariaDB
--      volume every run, so AUTO_INCREMENT always restarts at 1 — this is
--      NOT a "usually works" assumption, it is guaranteed by the harness's
--      own fresh-volume-per-run contract.
--
--   Net effect: `admin_user_id = 2` below IS the harness's own
--   `e2e_parity_admin` row (role 'super_admin', username 'e2e_parity_admin'
--   — see infra/e2e/seed/20-admin-user.sql.tmpl), by construction, every
--   single run. If a FUTURE batch's fixture (applied earlier in
--   FIXTURE_FILES, i.e. a lower-numbered file than this one) starts hitting
--   ANY auth_check.php-gated PHP page during ITS OWN seeding (none do today
--   — every existing fixture is pure SQL), that would change this id and
--   this file's `data_access_logs` row would need updating; a future author
--   changing FIXTURE_FILES' ORDER or adding an earlier HTTP-hitting seed
--   step should grep this file for `admin_user_id` and re-verify.
--
--   IMPORTANT CORROLARY (see docs/runbooks/phase2-settings-tabs-batch1-parity
